---
intent: >
  Bring `cli/init` into the new "writes brain.aide via `--brain <integration>`"
  shape. Default is `--brain obsidian`. Argument parsing fails fast on every
  retired backend-shaped flag (`--brain-path`, `--vault-path`, `--brain-root`,
  `--brain-token`, `--brain-url`, `--brain-name`) and on any unknown value
  passed to `--brain`. cli/init scaffolds `.aide/config/brain.aide` from the
  bundled template selected by `--brain` (today the only registered
  integration is `obsidian`, mapped to `obsidianBrainAideTemplate`) by
  invoking the shared install service and applying ONLY the brain.aide-scaffold
  InitStep. cli/init NEVER writes an `.mcp.json` brain entry, NEVER seeds the
  four entry-point artifacts, NEVER creates the brain root directory, and
  NEVER asks the user for a backend-specific value. `writeMcpEntry` shrinks
  to managing the `aide` key only. The terminal warning routes the user to
  `/aide:brain config` to fill the YAML null slot, derive the brain MCP
  entry through sync, and seed the entry-point artifacts. All retired tests
  are deleted; new tests assert the no-brain-wiring contract end-to-end.
---

