      template under `.claude/skills/`, the `aide` MCP server entry
      additively merged into `.mcp.json`, the `aide-tree` launcher at
      `.aide/bin/aide-tree.mjs`, the README badge, and the bundled
      `brain.aide` template selected by `--brain` at
      `.aide/config/brain.aide` (with YAML null at the unwired slot).
    - **What it does NOT do** (one paragraph): never writes a
      `.mcp.json` `brain` entry; never seeds the four entry-point
      artifacts (coding-playbook, study-playbook, update-playbook,
      research index); never creates the brain root directory; never
      asks for a brain path, token, connection URI, or any other
      backend-specific value; never accepts any backend-shaped flag
      (`--brain-path`, `--vault-path`, `--brain-root`, `--brain-token`,
      `--brain-url`, `--brain-name`).
    - **Recognized flags** (a list block):
      - `--help` — print this message and exit.
      - `--brain <integration>` — select which bundled template
        scaffolds. Today the only valid value is `obsidian` (the
        default when `--brain` is omitted). Future integrations land
        their own bundled templates and become valid `--brain`
        values without changing this contract.
      - `--ide <choice>` — select which IDE preview wiring
        scaffolds (preserved as-is; not implemented in this plan;
        see todo.aide carry-forward item).
    - **Post-install follow-up surfaces** (one short paragraph):
      brain wiring → run `/aide:brain config` on the first `/aide`
      run inside Claude Code; deferred IDE → re-run with
      `--ide <choice>`; skipped shipped artifacts → run
      `/aide:upgrade`.
    - **Forbidden vocabulary** in this text: `<BRAIN_PATH>`,
      `--brain-path`, `vault-path`, `brain-root`, `brain-token`,
      `brain-url`, `brain-name` — except where named explicitly as
      forbidden flags in the "what it does NOT do" paragraph (the
      sanctioned mention).
    - The text exits with `process.exit(0)`, matching today's IIFE
      shape.

